// The kanban board: a saved query's headings laid out in columns, with cards
// that turn over.
//
// A board owns nothing in the org files. Its columns, colours and card faces
// are a way of looking at headings the query found, and every card is worked
// out afresh each time the board is opened - so a heading edited in the editor,
// in another tab or by another person is right the next time this one refreshes
// rather than fighting a copy kept here. The two things a drag does write are
// the value the column stands for (a property, a tag or the todo keyword) and,
// when the board sorts by hand, one number on the card that moved.
//
// The model - which column a card lands in, what colour it takes, the order
// arithmetic - is in kanban.ts, and is pure. This file is the board: the
// layout, the drag, and the writes.

